    <item>
      <title>Why Is Asheville’s Buncombe County Jail Full of People?</title>
      <link>https://ashevillefm.org/post/why-is-ashevilles-buncombe-county-jail-full-of-people/</link>
      <description>Julie and Jeremy of the Asheville Community Bail Fund talk about the US system of pre-trial incarceration aka bail and bond, the work of the bail fund locally, the overcrowding of the Buncombe County Jail here in Asheville, the ICE holds happening in the local jail, and how local policy choices regarding criminalization are being compounded by recent and new North Carolina legislation.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://ashevillefm.org/post/why-is-ashevilles-buncombe-county-jail-full-of-people/</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://ashevillefm.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/tfsr-20260308-300x300.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Mar 2026 20:00:52 +0000</pubDate>
    </item>
